    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-01T21:16:30+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-01T21:16:30+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-01T11:46:30Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-01T11:46:30Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A cold front will move across SA on Tuesday. A high pressure ridge will move across the north of the state on Wednesday and Thursday and another cold front will slip across the southeast of SA early Thursday. The ridge will move eastwards early Friday then another trough will move over SA during the day followed by a cold front early Saturday. Another high pressure ridge will move across during Sunday ahead of a low pressure system expected to develop in the far west later in the day.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW015" description="Mount Lofty Ranges" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-01T21:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-02T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-01T11:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-01T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Slight chance of a shower. Winds west to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-02T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-03T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-01T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-02T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Slight chance of a shower. Winds west to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h tending west to northwesterly 25 to 30 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to around 9 with daytime temperatures reaching between 13 and 16.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:40am to 2:50pm, UV Index predicted to reach 5 [Moderate]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-03T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-04T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-02T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-03T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. High chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. Winds westerly 20 to 30 km/h becoming light in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 11 with daytime temperatures reaching between 13 and 17.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-04T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-05T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-03T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-04T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. The chance of morning fog in the south. Very high chance of showers, most likely in the afternoon and evening. Winds northerly 15 to 25 km/h turning northwesterly 25 to 35 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 8 with daytime temperatures reaching between 15 and 19.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-09-05T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-06T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-04T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-05T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. High chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. Winds northwesterly 25 to 40 km/h turning westerly during the morning then decreasing to 15 to 25 km/h during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to around 12 with daytime temperatures reaching between 13 and 17.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
